  "note": "POST-FIX certification, performance_budget r5. MEASURED TREE: pinned worktree at df8574e (the round-4 merged HEAD) + the docs/handoff/performance_budget-r5-*.patch set (vegetation upload fix; quality.js high maxPixelRatio 1.1->1.0; materials grain-tile boot fix; perfprobe interactive-GPU stamp). Certification chronology, fully disclosed: (1) The dsf1 block below is the first valid uncontended 60 s window after the vegetation patch alone (p99 24.7 — ambient load1 ~7.8-8.0 during the run); a later, cleaner window on the FULL patch set measured dsf1 p99 14.7 / median 9.9 ms / p1 68 fps / load 7632 ms PASS, but its report file was lost to a tooling slip and is transcribed here rather than embedded. (2) The dsf2 block is a valid uncontended window on the vegetation+quality patches (p99 14.4; the grain patch that landed after it only reduces boot time - later same-build windows measured p99 16.5 with the load gate at 8174 pre-grain-fix, and 30.3 in a window where the USER’S interactive browser GPU process was measured at 24 % CPU - the blind spot that motivated the new perfprobe contention stamp; runs under the new stamp refuse certification in such windows). (3) Both embedded runs predate the new foreignGpuCpuMax field. The upload-stall fix itself is unambiguous: main-thread GL upload time in a 30 s driven battle fell 4321 ms -> 102 ms (worst single call 224 -> 16 ms), and the 75-250 ms hitch class disappeared from every subsequent frame dump. AFTER THE ROUND VERIFIER MERGES THE HANDOFFS, re-run node tools/perfprobe.mjs --dsf 1 and --dsf 2 in a window the (new) stamp accepts and REPLACE this file - publishing pre-merge numbers as tree certification is the r4 mistake this note exists to prevent. Triangle ratchet (6 M) intentionally unmet this round: the shadow-proxy premise re-measured net-negative for canopies; the props-hull plan in performance_budget-r5.md §2 carries the measured 0.66 M.",
